# One regex per line. Any match in the tree (or in a built zip) fails the sweep.
# This file is public: it may only contain *shapes*, never a private value.
# A real IP, hostname, UUID, provider or person's name belongs in
# scripts/infra-sweep.denylist.local, which is gitignored and read as well
# when it exists. A denylist that publishes the values it protects is worse
# than no denylist at all.
#
# Tokens and keys by shape (a 64-hex agent token, a base64 WireGuard key literal)
[0-9a-f]{64}
[A-Za-z0-9+/]{43}=
# Shapes that betray a private deployment or a developer's machine
\bhomelab\b
@gmail\.com
/home/[a-z]+/
